Package: com.example.multifloat
Name: MultiFloat
Version: 0.10.0
Architecture: iphoneos-arm64e
Description: Multi-floating window / split-view tweak for iOS 17 (roothide / arm64e). 0.10.0 fixes the flicker that survived 0.9.1, and it is a self-inflicted bug, not a SpringBoard one. The decisive observation came from the user's own report on 0.9.1: lowering keepAliveMs to 100 or 50 made the flicker happen MORE OFTEN instead of shorter. If SpringBoard were the cause, polling faster could only shorten the black window, never make it more frequent; the frequency tracking our own period means we were the ones producing that black frame. The archive #10 log confirms it line by line (same pid 20257, one hosting round): deactivationReasons went non-zero 20+ times and in the large majority of them layers=2 and hosted=2 at the same time (the picture was fine); contentState went to 0 eleven times and in 8 of those the layers were intact; and layers=0, the only genuine black, happened just 4 times - every single one of them within 0-2 seconds AFTER one of our own updateSettingsWithBlock calls, with zero occurrences when we had not written. Writing settings makes SpringBoard recompute the whole settings object, the app's scene re-commits, contentState walks 2 -> 0 -> 1 -> 2 and the layers are rebuilt: that is the blink. 0.9.1 treated deactivationReasons != 0 as a drop, which on this device is true almost continuously, so it wrote on every tick and the blink frequency became exactly 1 / keepAliveMs. 0.10.0 therefore narrows the drop condition to one single quantity that directly means black - layerManager.layers <= 0 or the presenter host having zero hosted layers. deactivationReasons, contentState and idleModeEnabled are demoted to log fields (deact and idle are reported as an advisory that does nothing unless keepAliveSoft is turned on for A/B). Writes are now two-tiered: the default minimal write only sets idleModeEnabled=NO and deactivationReasons=0 (plus the frame if it has drifted), while setLevel: and setDisplayConfiguration: are demoted to an escalation step that is off by default, because they make SpringBoard recompute the entire settings object and setDisplayConfiguration: also resets the frame to the full screen 430x932 - one write buying two re-layouts. frame is always set last. Three brakes were added so a runaway loop is impossible: a grace period after mounting, a minimum interval between writes, and giving up after N consecutive failed ticks. The scene frame source of truth moved to panel.contentArea.bounds; 0.9.x read it from the presentation view's bounds, and since that view is resized to the full screen when hosting drops we kept writing 430x932 back into scene.frame, which is a positive feedback loop that also broke the aspect ratio. The view is now corrected at the view layer only, which touches no settings and causes no re-layout. Two log bugs are fixed as well: Chinese strings passed through %s are no longer mojibake, and processState/taskState/visibility are read with a 32-bit return type (0.9.1 printed ps=10751930112 because a 32-bit int was read as a 64-bit NSInteger). The capability report now scans UIApplication, the window scene, the FBScene, the scene handle and the presentation manager for an ivar holding a deactivation manager, so the next round can acquire UIApplicationSceneDeactivationAssertion and make the scene never get deactivated in the first place. Still no hooks are installed anywhere: only updateSettingsWithBlock:. Config defaults (override in /var/mobile/MultiFloat.plist): hostRoute 3, hostSceneFrame true, resizesHosted true, forceForeground true, keepAlive true, keepAliveMs 200, keepAliveSoft false, keepAliveDeact true, keepAliveIdle true, keepAliveLevel false, keepAliveForeground false, keepAliveMinWriteMs 300, keepAliveGraceMs 1500, keepAliveEscalateAfter 5, keepAliveGiveUpAfter 30, keepAliveFrameSync true, allowRouteB false, hostStep 6. cfgVersion=11, migrated once on first launch (keepAliveLevel true -> false, only while it still holds the old default). DISABLED BY DEFAULT for real hosting: needs enabled=true AND hostEnabled=true. Crash-guard marker still makes a crash loop impossible. Log: /var/mobile/MultiFloat.log
Maintainer: QingC12 <QingC12@users.noreply.github.com>
Author: QingC12
Section: Tweaks
Depends: firmware (>= 15.0)
